# Security

- Auth on every manager/API route. Agents authenticate with per-device credentials, not a shared password.
- CSRF on cookie session web POSTs; Bearer JWT or device tokens for the agent API.
- Parameterized SQL / ORM only. Escape all HTML output.
- Uploads: screenshots JPEG/WebP only, size cap, random names, no execution in storage dirs.
- Secrets in `.env` never committed. No production keys in docs.
- Server timestamps win over PC clock for attendance. Client clock is advisory only.
- Local agent DB is an **outbox**, not editable source of truth after sync.
- Employees can see their own day's status; they cannot rewrite signed punches after sync.
- TLS in production. Bind admin to LAN/VPN if hosted on-prem.
- Log access to screenshots (who viewed, when).
